**Bug (MAF-GAP-016):** The CLI hardcoded a hallucinated default model `gpt-5.1` (does not exist) in 5 source sites + 3 test files across `run-game.ts` / `config.ts` / `init.ts`, and the value violated the project's `provider/model` convention (`openai/gpt-4o-mini`). The CLI was sending a bare model name instead of a qualified provider/model string.

**Fix:** two global, case-sensitive replacements (order matters — the label contains `GPT-5.1` with a capital G, so it survives replacement #1 and is fixed by #2):

```bash
# 1) bare hallucinated model -> provider/model qualified name (5 src + 3 test sites)
perl -pi -e 's/gpt-5\.1/openai\/gpt-4o-mini/g' \
  src/run-game.ts src/config.ts src/init.ts \
  test/run-game.test.ts test/config.test.ts test/init.test.ts

# 2) choice label
perl -pi -e 's/GPT-5\.1 \(Recommended\)/GPT-4o mini (Recommended)/g' src/run-game.ts
```

Before/after per site:

```ts
// src/config.ts
- export const DEFAULT_MODEL = "gpt-5.1";
+ export const DEFAULT_MODEL = "openai/gpt-4o-mini";

// src/run-game.ts (choice list + CLI default/help)
- { value: "gpt-5.1", label: "GPT-5.1 (Recommended)" },
+ { value: "openai/gpt-4o-mini", label: "GPT-4o mini (Recommended)" },
- export const HELP_TEXT = "--model <provider/model> (default: gpt-5.1)";
+ export const HELP_TEXT = "--model <provider/model> (default: openai/gpt-4o-mini)";
- export async function selectModel(model: string = "gpt-5.1"): Promise<string> {
+ export async function selectModel(model: string = "openai/gpt-4o-mini"): Promise<string> {

// src/init.ts (generated config template)
- { model: "gpt-5.1", timeoutMs: 30_000 },
+ { model: "openai/gpt-4o-mini", timeoutMs: 30_000 },

// test/*.test.ts — assertions updated to expect "openai/gpt-4o-mini"
```

**Trapping pitfall:** never run `npx vitest run` from the repo root — there is no root vitest config. Always `cd apps/cli` first.
